  <info>
  <link type="guide" xref="accounting"/>
  <link type="seealso" xref="loans"/>
  <link type="seealso" xref="loan_payments"/>
  <desc>Pay a loan, split into principal and interest.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Loan payment</title>

  <p>Open <guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Loan payment</gui></guiseq>, or
  double click a loan payment in the main window's to-do list.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Loan</gui> and the <gui>Date</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Principal</gui> and choose the <gui>Loan
    account</gui> it pays down.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Interest</gui> and choose the <gui>Expense</gui>
    account it is charged to.</p></item>
    <item><p>Pay the total, as below.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <list>
    <item><p><gui>Pay with cash</gui>: choose the account it is paid
    <gui>from</gui> and click <gui>Cash payment</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Pay from bank account</gui>: choose the bank account. For a
    transfer, type the <gui>Transaction number</gui> and click
    <gui>Transfer</gui>. For a check, type its number and click
    <gui>Print</gui>; this records the check payment, it does not print a
    check.</p></item>
  </list>

  <p>The loan's next payment reminder moves on from today.</p>

</page>
